# Line endings.
#
# Anything copied into, or executed inside, a Linux container must keep LF. With
# core.autocrlf=true - the Windows default - a checkout would otherwise rewrite these to CRLF,
# and a CRLF shebang fails inside the image with
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# which breaks the workstation entrypoint for every contributor who clones on Windows. Git
# stores LF either way; this is about what lands in the working copy that `docker build` reads.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf

# The image and its tests in full, including the Maven settings the Dockerfile COPYs.
images/**       text eol=lf
tests/images/** text eol=lf
